<BaseLayout title="About | Which Deal's Better?" description="Learn why Which Deal's Better makes everyday unit-price and product-quantity comparisons faster.">
  <section class="content-section"><div class="shell prose"><p class="eyebrow">About the tool</p><h1>Shopping math, made quicker.</h1><p>Which Deal's Better? exists for the moment when two packages look similar, the shelf labels are confusing, and you just want a straight answer.</p><h2>What it does</h2><p>The calculator compares total price with total underlying quantity, including multipacks. It also converts compatible units so ounces can be compared with pounds, liters with milliliters, and more.</p><h2>Made for everyday decisions</h2><p>The tool is free, works on your phone, and requires no account. Calculator entries stay in your browser. The goal is simple: help you spend less time doing arithmetic in the aisle and make a more informed choice.</p><p><a class="primary-button" href="/">Compare deals now</a></p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
